<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korean strike status at 0500 GMT.</title>
<headline>South Korean strike status at 0500 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are the latest strike figures released by the Korean Confederation of Trade Unions.</p>
<p>Numbers are by industrial sector but include major companies in several sectors.</p>
<p>(Figures in brackets are Ministry of Labour estimates of actual workers on strike against the total workforce)</p>
<p>SECTOR	   STRIKING UNIONS	  STRIKERS</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Construction    6			   3,984</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Metal	    49			  50,251</p>
<p>Halla Heavy - 3,326 strikers (900/5,800)</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>University	3			     156</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Hospital	 24			  17,273</p>
<p>Seoul National - 2,093 strikers (200/4,000)</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Clerical	 12			   6,830</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Press	     4			   7,703</p>
<p>Korea Broadcasting - 4,800 strikers (1,500/6,224)</p>
<p>Munhwa Broadcasting - 2,200 strikers (1,800/3,289)</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Insurance	 1			   4,700</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Automobile     24			  53,388</p>
<p>Kia Motors - 17,000 strikers (9,200/29,389)</p>
<p>Asia Motors - 5,627 strikers (5,618/9,159)</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Professional   42			  14,717</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Other	     7			   1,803</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Hyundai Union  12			  82,085</p>
<p>Hyundai Motor - 34,008 strikers (18,000/41,125)</p>
<p>Hyundai Heavy - 21,700 strikers (150/27,000)</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Cheical 7 1,036</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>TOTAL	   189			 220,026</p>
<p>The Ministry of Labour puts the total number of strikers at 64,497 from 66 companies.</p>
</text>
